d Notion Skill page URL. Notion main reads inspect without adopting task instructions. Copy refs verbatim; never guess filesystem paths.\\n  path?: string;\\n  // Copy complete resource refs verbatim from the selected Skill snapshot's resource directory. Every ref must identify a file in the same owner and snapshot. Reads all selected files in one operation without preparing the main body.\\n  // @minItems 1 @maxItems 16\\n  paths?: Array<string>;\\n  // Use only for a user-requested current-version inspection; a successful complete read needs no follow-up refresh. Keeps the active selection unchanged. Only for a supplied Notion Skill ref in path; fixed resources and local files keep their versions.\\n  refresh?: boolean;\\n}): Promise<string | { data: string; mimeType: string; note: string; type: \\\"image\\\"; } | { effects?: { author_content: \\\"unchanged\\\"; remote_writes: \\\"none\\\"; version: 1; } | { author_content: \\\"unchanged\\\" | \\\"unknown\\\"; remote_writes: \\\"unknown\\\"; version: 1; }; files: Array<{ content: string; kind: \\\"text\\\"; path: string; ref: string; } | {\\n  // @integer @minimum 0\\n  bytes: number;\\n  kind: \\\"binary\\\";\\n  output: string;\\n  path: string;\\n  ref: string;\\n  sha256: string;\\n}>; status: \\\"ready\\\"; }>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"bash\",\"description\":\"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\\n\\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\\n\\ncodemode tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { bash(args: {\\n  // Shell command to execute\\n  command: string;\\n  // Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)\\n  timeout?: number;\\n}): Promise<{\\n  exit_code: number;\\n  // Full output, when truncated\\n  full_output_path?: string;\\n  // Combined stdout and stderr, possibly truncated\\n  output: string;\\n  truncated: boolean;\\n  wall_time_seconds: number;\\n}>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"edit\",\"description\":\"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.\\n\\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\\n\\ncodemode tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { edit(args: {\\n  // One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.\\n  edits: Array<{\\n    // Replacement text for this targeted edit.\\n    newText: string;\\n    // Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.\\n    oldText: string;\\n  }>;\\n  // Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)\\n  path: string;\\n}): Promise<string>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"write\",\"description\":\"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.\\n\\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\\n\\ncodemode tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { write(args: {\\n  // Content to write to the file\\n  content: string;\\n  // Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)\\n  path: string;\\n}): Promise<string>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"notion_list\",\"description\":\"Search the authorized Skill metadata directory, including items outside the default View. Returns Skill refs for read or notion_use; it does not load instructions or activate workflows. Use refresh:true to verify discovery after a write or request the latest directory; selected Skill versions stay fixed. Check freshness separately from coverage.\\n\\ncodemode tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { notion_list(args: {\\n  // Copy next_cursor to continue the same query and metadata publication; restart after refresh.\\n  cursor?: string;\\n  // Maximum metadata entries, default 20.\\n  // @integer @minimum 1 @maximum 100\\n  limit?: number;\\n  // A short name or description keyword; empty lists the directory.\\n  query?: string;\\n  // Refresh metadata for source, or all configured Notion sources when source is omitted. Keeps task pins; configured offline sources remain offline. Cannot combine with cursor.\\n  refresh?: boolean;\\n  // Optional configured source ID to disambiguate directories.\\n  source?: string;\\n}): Promise<string>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"notion_ctl\",\"description\":\"Inspect this branch's Skill graph or working_set. working_set show lists confirmed roots, Requires, visible instruction bytes and the session budget; budget explicitly sets max_bytes, null disables it; release retires only the supplied fixed roots and preserves shared Requires, Session history and Notion. Alternatively request cli_source for one exact configured Notion source's host-local CLI prefix when an authorized maintenance/source task needs it. These operations do not execute CLI commands or grant authorization. Choose only one operation.\\n\\ncodemode tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { notion_ctl(args: {\\n  // Exact enabled Notion source ID from host guidance. Return its host-local command prefix without execution; do not select a source implicitly.\\n  // @minLength 1\\n  cli_source?: string;\\n  // For budget only. Complete active instruction closure in UTF-8 bytes, not tokens. Explicit null disables the budget. No automatic eviction or truncation.\\n  max_bytes?: number | null;\\n  // Optional fixed sr:S/sr:R references to export as canonical identity and exact version proofs for independent validation.\\n  // @maxItems 64\\n  refs?: Array<string>;\\n  // For release only. Copy fixed root refs from working_set show or sele","type":"text"}],"details":{"calls":[]},"durationMs":61,"isError":false,"role":"toolResult","timestamp":1795431036849,"toolCallId":"call-[id:36f5907b57f1d4bf453e]-6|fc_75e688c2-890c-4717-a6c8-3e55308ca1df_0","toolName":"codemode"},"type":"message_start"},"episode_id":"benchmark-grok-4-7-unstarted-7-1-004","monotonic_ns":"35811319233333","request_id":"benchmark-grok-4-7-unstarted-7-1-004/request-3","run_id":"benchmark-grok-4-7-unstarted-7-1-004","sequence":245,"stage":"user_task","task_id":"no-skill-03-a-n16-r1","turn_id":"turn-1","type":"session_event","version":1,"wall_time":"2026-11-23T10:50:36.849Z"}
